        fignet05.darrins@eds.com (Darrin Smith) writes:
> Well, I need some opinions on the best (read cheap, easy,  and standard) 
> method to send files to and from the previously mentioned systems. 
> 
> I had thought of using FTP, and have the PC run something like Chameleon 
> but I'm not sure if VAX VMS supports FTP.  Does anyone know?

FTP is an option. VMS doesn't have 'native' support for tcp/ip, though there
are several options in the third party market and one from Digital.

They are:

CMU-IP, freeware
Multinet/VMS, from TGV
Pathway, from TWG
TCPWare, from Process Software
DEC TCP/IP Services for VMS

All of the above support FTP transfers. Our product goes quite a bit beyond
that, of course, but if all you need is FTP to move files around, look into
CMU-IP. No 'official' support, but it's free :)

