Bob McGuire wrote:
> 
>       zip bob.zip -V expdat.dmp
>       adding expdat.dmp (in=40960) (out=3396) (deflated 92%)
>       total bytes=40960, compressed=3396 -> 92% savings
> 

Bob,

Your problem is that OpenVMS lowercases all command line arguments when 
it passes them to a c program. You are using a "verbose" switch rather 
than a "save VMS file attributes" switch. You will need to quote it for 
it to work correctly.

eg. zip bob.zip "-V" expdat.dmp

If you really need to get the file back, you could try either convert 
(which will change the structure of the file and the file attributes) or 
a utility called file which is available from several web and ftp sites 
(it will only change the file header so that it thinks it has the 
correct structure). Try convert first (as you should have that already).

Rob Spencer



