Oh, my no.  A DECmate II is a dedicated word processor running a menuing
O/S called WPS.  Inside, it's a 12-bit PDP-8, although occasionally they
had a Z80 (?) coprocessor that could run CP/M programs.  There are several
variations of free operating systems you might like to try instead of WPS.
Check out the newsgroup alt.sys.pdp8, and most particularly the FAQ, for
pointers on how this can be done.

