Subject: DEC Alpha & TLZ06  makes tapes that HP1533 cannot find file marks
Date: 1996/02/24
Message-ID: <4gnlrj$2me@maggie-black.austin.wireline.slb.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 140964328
content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
organization: Schlumberger
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec
x-mailer: Mozilla 1.2N (Windows; I; 32bit)

I am troubleshooting a problem that appears to be related to a 
DEC Alpha & TLZ06 combination.  When I write tapes with this 
combination using a DLIS utility(utility that writes variable 
size blocks), I cannot read these tape correctly with an 
HP1533 tape drive.If I write the same tapes using a DEC Cougar 
& TLZ06, I have no problem reading the tapes with the HP1533. 
If I write the same tape with a KA655 & TLZ06 combination, I 
also do not have a problem reading the tape with the HP. What 
I have determined is that the HP1533 appears to be reading 
data correctly(using a binary dump) but does not find the 2nd 
file mark that indicates the end of data. If I write a tape 
with a TLZ07 & Alph,Cougar,or KA655, I do not have a problem 
reading the tape with the HP1533. This scenario has been 
tested with multible HP1533s, TLZ07s, and TLZ06s.

I have no problem changing to TLZ07s but I am faced with 
thousands of tapes that have been written with the Alpha & 
TLZ06 combination.

Has anyone experienced a similar situation to mine?  Any 
suggestions would be appreciated.

James Luhn
luhn@slb.com




