fignet05.darrins@eds.com (Darrin Smith) wrote:

>Well, I need some opinions on the best (read cheap, easy,  and standard) 
>method to send files to and from the previously mentioned systems. 

>I had thought of using FTP, and have the PC run something like Chameleon 
>but I'm not sure if VAX VMS supports FTP.  Does anyone know?

>You can either respond directly to me, or post to this group.

>Thanks.

VAX/VMS does support FTP, but only if you purchase something like
TCPware or UCX, which are TCP/IP products and are quite expensive if
you only want to copy the odd file.  However, these are "standard"
methods.  I use TCP/IP products (TCPware in fact) but for very fast
and very stable PC to VAX/VAX to PC  transfers I use the Reflection 4
terminal emulation product.  Reflection supports both Windows 3.1 and
NT, and will communicate over LAT or TCP/IP.  For the fastest transfer
use their Network Stack.

I hope this helps


Ashley Shepherd




