I picked up a VAXStation II at a local computer auction recently, and
being very new to the world of VAXen, I need a bit of help to get the
machine doing something.

1)	Can I use my VR201 console as the system console? If so, what cable
do I need to use with it (i.e. can I get away with a straight-through
15-pin DB15F-DB15F?)? 

2)	My machine powers up, and eventually the RUN light comes on and the
7-segment display in the back says A. I've got a M7606 CPU board. What
does this mean?

3)	Is the DB9M connector for a console terminal pinned out just like a
PC DB9 serial connector? If not, how would I wire a cable to connect it
to a PC's serial port?

4)	I heard a rumor that there is some jumper or switch called `S3'
somewhere in the box that causes the console terminal port to be the
default console instead of the console port. Where is this jumper on my
machine?

5)	I think that this system was booted from tape in a previous life,
since the system doesn't seem to read off the HD after the ready light
pops up. So, where can I get a tape with any kind of OS that I can boot
off of? I'm thinking of running NetBSD/VAX, since it's got no licensing
fees of any sort, but I need a means of loading the boot/root image onto
