ULTRIX 4.3 machine (5000/200) and it runs spectacularly.  I had problems
getting NCSA to pre-fork processes, but Apache works great.  I like its
idea of keeping a certain number of "spares" around as opposed to NCSA's
static pool of processes.  

It can be gotten (with good documentation) from www.apache.org or ftp.apache.org

