In article <206196374wnr@falstaf.demon.co.uk>, Robin Birch <robin@falstaf.demon.co.uk> writes:

>Dear All,
>I am installing some spare hitachi disks that I have got onto a 3100
>running ultrix.  Has anybody got a partition scheme for these.  The most
>important info is the number of tracks, sectors, sizes etc.  I don't
>have any paperwork unfortunately.

If you are running ULTRIX V4.0 or later and the disk puts its geometry
in a conventional place, ULTRIX can get the geometry for you.  One of
these should work:

# newfs /dev/rrz#a /dev/rrz#a

or:

# newfs /dev/rrz#a hitachi

The driver will also use a default partition table and newfs will write
the default to the disk.  Then, if you need to, you can repartition as
you like.

