Sally Han wrote:
>
> If anyone can enlighten me with the pro's and con's of clustering
> 2 VAX 4000 Model 600's as a DSSI cluster vs. a CI cluster, please
> email me at sally.han@nb.rockwell.com.  If you have any horror or
> success stories that are relevant to this issue, I would really
> like to hear about them.  Any and all help would be greatly
> appreciated!
>Unless you have an overwhelming reason for going to CI, stick with 
DSSI clustering.
1. It is a fully supported solution, with no finger pointing between
   vendors.
2. Much higher performance - 4 DSSI buses at 4 MB/sec/bus 
   vs 2.6 MB/sec tops for the Q bus, and no worries about contention
   for the Q bus.
The HSD10 gives DSSI-SCSI connectivity at reasonable price and 
performance, the HSD30 gives a lot more features at a much higher
cost. I believe CMD do some good controllers, but I have no experience
with them.
The CIQBAs have had their problems in the past, with compatibility 
with new Digital CI nodes. A site I worked at recently which uses
CIQBAs had crashes with some non-conclusive evidence pointing to 
the CIQBA. However, they generally work OK, and if you have a stack of
CI storage gear available inhouse, it is a reasonable solution. I just
would not consider buying CI gear for a small (2-3 node) cluster.
-- 
