>
>   It's my understanding that G++ new and free use the malloc() out of
>   DEC's standard C library, so I'm not sure if it's a problem with the
>   DEC malloc() or the G++ environment...hence the crossposting.  Not
>   having the source to malloc(), I can't exactly debug it myself.
>
>   Does anybody know what's going on here, or if there is a patch for
>   malloc() or gcc?  Thanks!
>
