A simple program like this can generate those type of messages.
I suspect that you are freeing memory you don't own or are trying
to free part of a block of memory. 

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
 
 
main(int argc, char **argv)
{
        char *mem;
        char *mem2;
 
        mem = malloc(10);
        free (&mem[2]);    /* free unallocated memory - messes up heap */
        mem2 = malloc(10);
}

On the DEC Alpha machines we have here, it generates:

Unaligned access pid=30307 <a.out> va=1400028fa pc=3ff800cd4c8 ra=3ff8010dae4 type=ldq
Unaligned access pid=30307 <a.out> va=1400028e2 pc=3ff800cd820 ra=3ff8010dae4 type=ldq

