Alan Winston writes:
>Folks --
>
>I have RZ29B drives sitting in the StorageWorks shelf on my AlphaServer 2100,
>which is running OVMS 6.2.  It has a SWXCR three-channel PCI-SCSI RAID
>controller.  Anyway, the firmware revision on these drives is 7, which I
>understand is known to cause silent data loss.
>
>The system is not yet commissioned, so I can shut it down and take the drives
>away if I need to.
>
>How can I get the firmware upgraded?  Supposedly there is a utility for Unix on
>Alpha, but not for VMS.  I hear also that there is one for an Intel PC with
>Adaptec SCSI controller, and we have one of those.  Does anybody know where I
>can download that utility (the PC utility), or if there actually is a VMS
>utility someplace?  The DEC guy who does tech support for DOE laboratories was
>going to do this, but no luck so far.

Digital does have a SCSI tool for VMS if you are running VMS 6.2 (actually
there is another one for VMS V6.1, but you have to beg CSC for it).

Download patch ALPSCSI02_062, in this kit there is an RZTOOLS_ALPHA image
that can be used to load firmware upgrades and provide other SCSI
information on your drives.  It is available at Digital's ftp site
(ftp.service.digital.com/pub/vms/v6.2/alpscsi02_062.a-dcx_axpexe).

If you can find the firmware patch you need for the RZ29, you will be able
to do it on the VMS system. 

