I don't know how many years ago this was, but some cautions should
be noted: The basic LAT protocol hasn't changed much over the years, but 
some additions have been made to deal with things like running X protocol 
over the LAT transport (so-called "service class 3", I think).  If all 
you're interested in is old-fashioned terminal I/O, then any old spec 
will probably work.  If you're interested in newer features, I'm not so 
sure...

Don't take my words as gospel.  They really just represent random 
thoughts now.  I haven't worked with LAT for 7 years.
