In article <4fklo7$kd5@tst.hk.super.net>, jackyh@news.hk.super.net
(Mr Jacky Ho) writes:

:...We are asking for migration path, a smooth and realistic one. 
:...Anyone having similar experience ?  Is the conversion easy ?

  If your performance and configuration is sufficient for your current
  and planned needs, you need not consider migration to a faster OpenVMS
  VAX system, or to an OpenVMS Alpha system.  (PDP-11s are still in use
  at a number of customer sites, and new PDP-11s are available...)  If,
  on the other hand, I did need an upgrade, I'd seriously consider an
  OpenVMS Alpha system...

	--

  Though this was posted in comp.sys.dec, I'll assume this is OpenVMS.

  There are migration manuals in the OpenVMS Alpha documentation -- for
  system management, for Macro32 code, and for planning for the migration,
  and there exists a VAX C to DEC C migration manual in the DEC C manual
  set. 

  In my experience, the conversion is generally far easier than it might
  seem, and with mixed-architecture VMSclusters, one can "stage" the
  conversion work into production.

  The conversion itself can be made via DECmigrate (VEST), it can be made
  via recompilation and relink (there is a Macro32 compiler available for
  compiling VAX assembler into Alpha code), or it may require source code
  changes.  I've got the same (_large_) code base running on both platforms,
  and I noticed only a few areas where the Bliss-Macro-C code base had some
  platform-dependencies -- these areas were (in my case) easily removed.

  (Most source code can be simply recompiled and relinked -- though some of
  the compilers have been known to flag latent errors in the source code. 
  Unless the code is tied into a feature specific to the VAX architecture
  -- carnal knowledge of the stack frame is one such area, and privileged
  mode code that accesses platform-specific data structures is another --
  the application programming interfaces are compatible between the two
  platforms and the source code need not see any changes.)

  There is also some information on this topic in the OpenVMS Frequently
  Asked Questions (FAQ) posting.  The FAQ is posted here monthly, and is
  archived in the following locations:

    comp.answers newsgroup
    news.answers newsgroup
    ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms
    ftp://rtfm.mit.edu/pub/usenet/news.answers/dec-faq/vms
    CompuServe VAXFORUM, Library 0, VMSFAQ.TXT

