In article <4fbhu8$ge4@central.server.swt.edu>, lh04@nyssa.swt.edu writes:
:I am trying to connect VT-320's to Decserver 100/200's....and the usual 3 wire 
:Send,Receive,Ground will not work????? The MMJ(yuck) has 6 lines in but do you 
:really need any more than the usual 3 for terminals that interface via DB-25?
:Lige - lige@txlutheran.edu

  I'd certainly connect all of the appropriate pins -- floating grounds can
  cause some rather interesting communications problems.  Easiest solution
  is to pick up some new/used MMJ adapters, and some cable, and connect the
  adapters to the DECservers -- MMJ and similar telco-parts-based schemes
  are (IMNSHO) far more convenient than the traditional DB25 RS232 wiring.

  The MMJ pinout is listed in the OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
  monthly posting, as are the adapter part numbers, as are the cable part
  numbers.  The FAQ is available at the following locations:

    comp.answers newgroup
    news.answers newsgroup
    ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms
    ftp://rtfm.mit.edu/pub/usenet/news.answers/dec-faq/vms
    CompuServe VAXFORUM, Library 0, VMSFAQ.TXT

