>Can anyone tell me a little about the VAX 
>stations (VXT 2000) that I have recently been exposed to??

The VXT 2000 is almost like a diskless VAXstation.  It has a VAX SOC
processor running at 25-30 Mhz, built in ethernet and serial IO, and
either a 2-bit greyscale or 8-bit accelerated color (SPX) graphics
controller.

As far as I know DEC never released VMS or Ultrix for this product,
just the standalone X terminal software.

