Just for those who may be curious I've resolved my problem with
aliases under MicroVMS 4.1M. Having run ANAL/DISK/REPAIR I discovered
some "Incorrect Backlinks" which I fixed by hand. I subsequently
discovered that these are _meant_ to be present and are a side-effect
of aliases (read hard-links) in the filesystem.

Reinstalling from tape and investigating, then restoring the system, I
discovered that the aliases in question were:

DUA0:[000000]SYSMAINT.DIR;1 <-> DUA0[000000.SYS0]SYSMAINT.DIR;1

and

DUA0:[000000.SYS0.SYSEXE]SYSBOOT.EXE;1 <-> DUA0:[000000.SYSEXE]SYSBOOT.EXE;1

These have subsequently been fixed with SET FILE/ENTER

Thanks to all those that helped ... my VMS knowledge is slightly
improved now! Still a long way to go ...

Cheers,

Bob.
