You can't boot VMS from a tape. What you can do is boot stand-alone 
backup from a tape, and then use it to restore a VMS image from tape to 
a disk.  You then boot the VMS disk.

Later machines have console commands to display the configuration.  
Unfortunately, the MVII does not.  If you boot the VMS diagnostics 
tape, it will make an attempt to identify the installed boards.

If you've been moving boards around, the most likely cause of boards 
not responding (which had previously responded) is that the Q-bus 
interrupt chain is broken.  Going from right to left on the backplane. 
Each slot must be filled. Starting at the third (8 slot backplane) or 
fourth (12 slot backplane) slot, both the top and bottom of the slots 
must be filled.

Good luck!

