|>
|>Folks- what is the endianess of the DEC Alpha machines?

Digital's Alpha systems are little-endian.  (The Alpha processor can be
used in either little-endian or big-endian modes, but as far as I know, the
big-endian mode has been used only in certain Cray products using Alpha
chips.)

DEC Fortran has a -convert big_endian compile switch which will cause data
to be converted automatically during unformatted I/O.  
