naturally):

	Num of units	CSR	VEC1	VEC2	Comments
PUA	1		772150	774	000	MSCP Disk controller
PTA	1		774500	260	000	TK50 controller
XQA	1		774440	120	000	DEQNA
TTA	4		760100	300	304	DZQ11

Now, it seems to me that the TK50 and DEQNA controllers are set to
their default CSR/VEC, whereas the MSCP controller seems to have a
wierd vector, rather than the standard 154. This is a floating vector
under software control, so I don't know whether this is OK or not. The
DZQ11 seems to have the default CSR and VEC for the 2nd such
controller, but changing back to the factory settings for a single
DZQ11 prevents it from being recognised by VMS. Comments anyone?

The machine itself is aranged like so (looking from the back, onto the
top of the boards).

         ----------------------------------------------

