newsgroups: alt.sys.pdp11,comp.sys.dec,vmsnet.pdp-11


Thanks to all those here who have helped me out over the past couple
of weeks. The problem of erratic operation of my TK50 magtape unit (in
particular, VMS claiming that the unit was off-line in the middle of
tape access operations) now seems to have been solved.

Having investigated earthing the system, CSRs, vectors, VMS sysgen
settings etc, etc, I discovered that the TK50 worked fine without the
lid fitted, but failed sporadically with the lid in place. I've now
left the lid off the drive and reassembled the machine. So far I've
seen now problems!

Seems the TK50 is a notoriously unreliable drive and is very sensitive
to any friction between the tape, the mechanism and the lid. A good
clean out probably helped too ...

Cheers,

Bob.
