Alexi,

There are quite a few considerations to be made before you can arrive
at a decision regarding the DEC Alpha systems.  You say you need 100 GB
of disk.  I would hope you intend to run some level of RAID on this
large of an array.  To that end, I suggest you consider one of
Digital's controllers, especially the HSZ40 family.  Using a single
HSZ, you will easily be able to configure 100 GB of disk running RAID
0, 1, 0+1, or 5.  To keep your price reasonable while giving you the
most for your dollar, I would recommend that you take a look at the
line of AlphaServer 1000 or even the AlphaServer 400 family of
machines.  Should you decide to go with the HSZ, another cost you will
have to consider is a StorageWorks cabinet.  In your case (but
depending on your need for scalibility), I would suggest the SW500-FA
cabinet.  Feel free to contact me at malz_w@declne.enet.dec.com if you
have any further questions.

Will



