X-Deja-AN: 137846807
organization: Naval Undersea Warfare Center, Newport, RI
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Solid State Disk Drive Reliability/Hot Swapping-

We have a Quantum ESP580 solid state SCSI disk drive sitting in a BA350 storage
works box on a pair of CMD Hawk Controllers.  These are connected through
a Star Coupler over the CI to a VAXCluster running VMS 6.1.  When removed
from its location and placed in another BA350 box, the drive becomes unavailable
and shows up as "busy" on the controller. Normally, this drive is not moved
from its location, but on a loss of power, or a power surge (we are working
on getting a UPS), the same error occurs.  Once this error condition does
occur, our vendor must take this disk offsite to do a low level format. Has
anyone seen similar error conditions in these or the Digital equivalent drive?
Are these drives "hot swappable?"  Is anyone in a similar configuration
experiencing similar problems?   Is there anything we can do on site to
alleviate this situation?

Thanks for your help...

Tom (NOEL@NPT.NUWC.NAVY.MIL)



