|>Oughtn't an error in a "write(unit,*)" statement, where no "err=" has
|>been specified, cause an abort in the same manner as "write(unit,fmt)"
|>does?

Yes, it should.  We recently identified a bug in the RTL that causes this
behavior - expect to see it corrected in the RTL that ships with the next
version of DEC Fortran. 
