Do you really need to define all of the users to groups like this?  This is
only needed if you intend to switch groups (ie using newgroup).  If this is
their login group (as specified in the /etc/passwd file), then you do not
need to respecify them in /etc/group.  The line in the /etc/group file can
just be 'problem storing 3000 soft:*:3000:' to give the group a name.

If you do need to specify them to switch groups, then you are in trouble due
to the NIS restriction (as previously stated).

Tom Merrick
Ohio State University

