In article <1996Jan27.195043@dax>, wade@dax.asub.arknet.edu writes:
>I have an LN03 printer that gives an error 2 on power up with the
>service dude flashing.  Can anyone tell me what this is and what to
>check.

Error code 2 with the little man indicates that you have an optical system
error.

The most common cause of this is that the +24v interlock is broken somewhere in
the printer.  

Open the left door, and locate the 2 shiny pins on the door.  They are the
interlock.  Note where they mate with a connector when the door is shut.  Make
sure the connections are clean.  There is another one of these connectors on
the development drawer on the left side.  

I usually see this error after adding toner (with the drawer pulled out).  It
usually comes from not pushing the drawer back in firmly.

How's things in Beebe?  Both of my parents are from there, and I still have
several relatives in Searcy and in Ward.

