Tripp Lilley (tltest@perspex.com) wrote:
: 1) I want more RAM, anywhere from 8 to 20 megs more. What's the best
: 	approach? add/replace/throw away :)

If you have 12MB now, you'll need to pull out 4MB (2 x 2MB SIMMs) and
add as many as 2 pairs of 8MB SIMMs (for either 24MB or 40MB, total).
I believe that Digital Basics sells refurb memory for the 5000/25, 
pretty cheap.  DEC might still be selling refurbs, too.

: 2) I want a second ethernet device (TurboChannel?) so I can make this
: 	box route! Again, what's the best approach.

Buy a Turbochannel ethernet adaptor.  Digital Basics has 'em for a 
couple hundred bucks.  I use my 5000/25 as a router in this very manner.
I think the part number is PMAD-AA...

: 3) Is there a good multiport serial card? Adding terminals *without*
: 	a separate terminal server would be interesting...

There are several, but they are quite costly -- getting a used DECserver 
200MC/300/700 is generally *much* cheaper.  If you use LAT, you can make 
all of the ports appear to be plain old tty devices on the DECstation,
if that's your desire.  If you get the 300 or 700, you can use TCP/IP, 
instead.

