In article <9601311638.AA07873@synchrods.synchrods.COM>, daniel@synchrods.synchrods.com (Daniel Senderowicz) writes:
> However I'm now having a different problem: The TK50 is stuck,
> the red light keeps blinking, so I push it in and out a few
> times, then it settles, it seems to make the tape move for a
> couple of seconds and after a while goes back into the blinking
> mood. The main problem is that as it is now I can't remove the
> tape in which I have the system. Is there any way to reset this,
> and/or taking the tape out without resorting to placing the
> device under the wheels of my diesel truck? Thanks in advance,

  This means the drive has faulted. You can try to force an unload by
pushing the red button in and out a few times (I believe the exact
pattern is out/in/out/in/out, assuming it's in to start with). That
will tell the drive electronics to ignore the controller card and any
communication faults and just unload the tape. It may take a while to
unload if the tape isn't at BOT.

  You will probably get the tape stuck again if you try it again, so
you should either find someone to test your drive and controller or
try swapping them (if you have spares).

