In article <4er74k$8vb@kryten.awinc.com>, C. Giroux <cgiroux@awinc.com> wrote:
>We're looking at getting a DEC Alpha machine which, as far as I
>know, is called Easy Internet Server or something like that.  It
>has a 256K cache and comes with windows NT.  Can anybody give me
>their opinion of this machine?  I am totally unfamiliar with this
>architecture.  We had planned to run Unix, but this machine was
>priced better.
>

Methinks what you're looking is a Multia "universal desktop client." 
Multias come with either 166 MHz or 233 MHz 21066 processors, minimum 
24MB of memory, and at least ~345MB of disk. On a bang-for-the-buck 
basis, Multia trounces the AlphaStation 200 4/100.


